I was playing around in wizard mode, and decided just for the hell of it
to see if I could buy an absurd intrinsic AC.  I teleported to the shrine
in mine town, and sadly, found that it was neutral (I was a chaotic elf)...
Being annoyed, I decided to toast the priest with my +60 stormy (I conjured
up a shield of reflection to avoid problems with backlash and angry gods,
though I suppose I could have just refused to die...)  I got the typical
message about the neutral god being mad...  I checked my status, and sure
enough, I had sinned...  Now, I could see my chaotic god being pissed if
I killed a coaligned friendly, but this was a differently-aligned priest...
He should have been happy.  He should be happy when I toast peaceful watch
captains.  I'm furthering the cause of chaos!

Anyway, I decided to try to appease the bastard, so I grabbed the aligned
priest corpse and stood on the altar.  I figured offering a priest corpse
would work regardless, since it was, after all, a neutral priest's corpse,
so conversion shouldn't be a possibility, right?  Wrong...  My god gets
pissed, and the neutral god accepts my allegiance.  Hmmm, thinks I, no matter,
I'll just sacrifice an elf (me being an elf) and become evil...  Nope!  My new
neutral god is now pissed at me, too!

I went back and tried again, this times using elf corpses, and the altar
converted smoothly, and I was accepted back into the fold...

Bizarre...

